abstract: Tong ren tang zheng xin lu is an 1837 accountability register of Shanghai’s
  Tongrentang charity, recording relief rules, donations, rents and accounts for widow
  and elderly support, coffins, charitable burial and emergency water provision. It
  supports research on Qing urban charity, relief governance and charitable property.
  Using Bodleian Libraries Sinica 690, this dataset provides AI-collated text for
  all 140 source images in JSON, TXT and TEI, retaining original characters, column
  and reading order, stable units, uncertainties and revision history. This AI-collated
  version retains uncertainties, has not undergone human or expert collation, and
  includes a limited punctuation layer that remains independently unreviewed. This
  revision applies 4 source-supported character corrections following targeted non-blind
  review of reader proposals; it is not a new full-book independent collation.
